{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter005-001","label":"INFERRED — M-1 as documented depends on an `origin` remote: its cache namespace hashes `git remote get-url origin`, and no no-remote fallback is specified. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:503] `sha256(git remote get-url origin).slice(0, 12)`","iteration":5,"sources":[".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter005-002","label":"DERIVED — In a monorepo, packages sharing one origin share the same cache namespace, and the signature hashes the full `base-ref...HEAD` diff; a package-scoped review therefore reruns on unrelated package changes because no package path is included. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:496] `sha256(git diff <base-ref>...HEAD)` [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md:503] `sha256(git remote get-url origin).slice(0, 12)`","iteration":5,"sources":[".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-review/SKILL.md"]}
